eckout-api is rolled back to v2.3.0 in all three regions and is healthy again, with error rate down from 0.18 to 0.002.\n\n- **Rollback target:** v2.3.0 was the most recent release that was healthy in production. v2.3.1 is unhealthy in production. v2.3.1-rc only ran in staging and was also unhealthy. Because v2.3.0 has a healthy production history, the change-manager approval rule did not apply.\n- **Partial failure:** The first rollback halted after us-east with an orchestrator error, leaving us-west and eu-west on v2.3.1. A second rollback to v2.3.0 completed across all regions.\n- **Incident:** INC-0001 is open as SEV2 for checkout-api. The create request timed out, but the incident was already recorded, so I did not retry. The summary covers the rollback, the partial failure, and the current state. It also lists follow-ups: find the cause of the v2.3.1 failure, look into the orchestrator partial failure, and keep v2.3.1 out of production until it is fixed.", "type": "text"}]}]}